# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Raw data stays out of git: the UCI workbook is 45MB and `python run_demo.py`
# downloads it on demand. A 500-row sample is committed under data/sample/.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
data/raw/
*.xlsx
*.zip
*.parquet
# ...except the baseline profile store, which the served model needs (see below).
!models/customer_profiles.parquet

# Charts and evidence tables in reports/ ARE committed -- the README embeds them
# and they are the submission's evidence. One exception:
# scratch images written by the notebooks
reports/nb_*.png

# The baseline model, its profile store and the scored book ARE committed, at a
# combined 2MB. They are build artifacts by nature -- `make demo` regenerates all
# three in ~35s -- but a hosted deploy clones the repo and never runs the pipeline,
# so excluding them means the dashboard boots with no model and the Portfolio and
# Policy screens render empty. A demo that works on a fresh clone is worth 2MB.
# Anything trained from the dashboard stays out; that is per-deployment data.

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/
env/

# Tooling
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Editors / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
.qodo/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Runtime decision ledger. Regenerated by serving traffic, not a build artifact --
# and it is per-deployment evidence, so it does not belong in version control.
audit/

# Bring-your-own-data: uploads and the results of running on them. Per-deployment
# artifacts, not build outputs -- the committed baseline lives in reports/.
data/uploads/
reports_user/
models_user/
audit_user/
data/datasets/

# Local working files: the UI reference mock and the generated design preview.
Screenshot*.png
reports/ui_preview.html
